thern I-25 Corridor including Walsenburg and\nTrinidad.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM this afternoon to 11 PM MST this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Be prepared for winter driving conditions. Slow down and\nuse caution while traveling.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Heavy bands of snow will develop across the\nsoutheast mountains and into the southern I-25 Corridor through the\nlate afternoon and evening. Quick bursts of moderate to heavy snow\ncan be expected, leading to near white out conditions, quick snow\naccumulations and dangerous travel conditions through the evening.","ends":"2026-11-23T23:00:00-07:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.430d907d8b37c6f34197c5a3cbe44407496d50e8.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.430d907d8b37c6f34197c5a3cbe44407496d50e8.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-23T19:33:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231933 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1233 PM MST Mon Nov 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered snow showers expected across the mountains/valleys today, with a few showers spilling onto the plains this evening and overnight. - Any accumulating snowfall today/tonight looks light, with spotty 1-3 inches amounts over the mountains and generally less","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-23T08:05:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 230805 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 105 AM MST Mon Nov 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-240815- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosq","url":"https://fore